<div id="35c7a374"><section id="frequently-asked-questions" class="B_EDxoOxVgAU8kPXBQWa"><h2 class="FrR9v_ssranAjR5kDzwF Lz7bstkpq5d6FanMqkLu">Frequently asked questions</p>
</h2><div class="XmC_S2INgPyqbncnXLoy XL4KGq1qGQz8WwtKJ_pg"><div class="YKYBQ3jDmxdtO9SEemuL"><div class="uJgrlGAPM7ozrDvgjXt0"><ul class="csX3C9e9jiZog4fiK1f5"><li><div class="zsrYitxhmI4Rdxl8AcId te60PfIJAvlwZ2RBbGqe o80VkuFKdpLspcd2K6XW"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="AccordionItem__46680" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT GNG_gRf6Dl3NsaHoWAUO OyyOerhMVj5mV5WQNX5V xZxJs8W876NY1tCMuMwq UM1jfJqOS1COdaoBDFKC"><div class="YSRmfctHOQ5noBfQfMH5"><div class="DnD1xRazitrvmLCwsQvo"><h3 class="Y1lcLNcJwl0MgDDEuPIe">What are the admission requirements?</h3></div><span class="SvgIcon MFUfNtxb_KMTBmiHESl8"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-plus"></use></svg></span></div></button><div style="will-change:height;overflow:hidden;visibility:hidden;height:0" class="ZgXVgEgkOVHpOr6mpnZu"><div id="AccordionItem__46680" class="pxYchGNIM3U95N_8sY2T"><div class="BcPDQdbKyOolxjjq14w1"><div class="RichtextContent">A Master&rsquo;s degree in Design builds upon a bachelor&rsquo;s degree or other equivalent education amounting to 180 ECTS, with at least 80 ECTS relevant to the chosen specialization.</p>
<p>For the specialization in Interior Architecture, a bachelor&rsquo;s degree in Interior Architecture is required.</p>
<p>For the specialization in Visual Communication Design, applicants with a bachelor&rsquo;s degree in Graphic Design, Illustration, Art Direction, Interaction Design, Animation, or similar fields may apply.</p>
<p>Kristiania may, in accordance with the<span>&nbsp;</span>Regulations on Requirements for Master&rsquo;s Degrees, approve other documented qualifications&mdash;such as relevant professional experience&mdash;that are wholly or partially equivalent to these requirements in special cases.<br /><br /><strong>Language requirements</strong><br />Applicants with education from outside the Nordic countries must document their proficiency in English, in terms of speaking and writing. You can meet the English language requirements by completing one of the following tests:&nbsp;</p>
<ul class="Richtext__ul">
<li>English (140 hours) from Norwegian upper secondary school: written and oral exam.</li>
<li>TOEFL with a minimum of 500 points from TOEFL PBT (paper-based test) or 60 points from TOEFL IBT (internet-based test).</li>
<li>IELTS academic test with a minimum score of 5.0.</li>
<li>PTE Academic, academic test with a minimum score of 51.</li>
<li>Cambridge ESOL Examinations: First Certificate in English, Certificate in Advanced English, Certificate of Proficiency in English.</li>
</ul>
<p>You can also meet the English requirements if you have completed one of the following:&nbsp;</p>
<ul class="Richtext__ul">
<li>A university degree in English language and literature</li>
<li>A minimum of one year of university studies taught in English in one of these countries: Australia, Canada, Ireland, New Zealand, Great Britain, or the USA.</li>
<li>Completed a bachelor&rsquo;s degree where the language of instruction was English</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Separate admission requirements for the program &ndash; entrance exam</strong><br />The entrance exam is as follows:&nbsp;<br /><br /></p>
<p>1. Application Letter that sets out the applicant's academic area of interest, goals,&nbsp;and motivation for applying to the program/specialization, as well as a&nbsp;preliminary description of the theme for the master's project. The heading must&nbsp;reflect the specialization the candidate is applying for. The application lettershould include:</p>
<p>a. Motivation and goals for applying to the program.<br />b. Presentation of the desired theme for design exploration in the master's<br />project, including the background for your interest in the theme, the<br />theme's societal relevance, suggestions for a problem statement/research<br />questions that delimit the theme, methods/process frameworks, and<br />theory/knowledge base.</p>
<p>The theme is not binding for the entire master's period but will guide the<br />assignment of your master's supervisor. The application letter should not exceed&nbsp;800 words.</p>
<p>2. 3-6 Works Samples that demonstrate the applicant's artistic and academic level within the specialization they are applying for. Describe the themes and&nbsp;frameworks of the works/projects with a brief introduction. Explain the process&nbsp;and methods in at least one of the works. Work samples can be supplemented&nbsp;with attached files (e.g., video, audio, etc.) or a URL to a website where they are&nbsp;adequately presented.</p>
<p>3. CV. The CV should detail education and work experience, independent<br />artistic/design activities, and other competencies/experience.</p>
<p>4. Diplomas and/or Other Documentation of formal Competence in higher<br />education. This documentation must be submitted in two places, so the<br />admissions committee can assess the education as part of the admission<br />evaluation, and so the formal admission requirement is documented. These<br />documents must be stored separately in our systems.</p>
<p>Applicants who qualify for the second admission round through the first round will be&nbsp;invited to a mandatory interview and/or additional admission test in the chosen&nbsp;specialization. Further information will accompany the invitation to the second&nbsp;admission round.</div></div></div></div></div></li><li><div class="zsrYitxhmI4Rdxl8AcId te60PfIJAvlwZ2RBbGqe o80VkuFKdpLspcd2K6XW"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="AccordionItem__46681" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT GNG_gRf6Dl3NsaHoWAUO OyyOerhMVj5mV5WQNX5V xZxJs8W876NY1tCMuMwq UM1jfJqOS1COdaoBDFKC"><div class="YSRmfctHOQ5noBfQfMH5"><div class="DnD1xRazitrvmLCwsQvo"><h3 class="Y1lcLNcJwl0MgDDEuPIe">What equipment will I need?</h3></div><span class="SvgIcon MFUfNtxb_KMTBmiHESl8"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-plus"></use></svg></span></div></button><div style="will-change:height;overflow:hidden;visibility:hidden;height:0" class="ZgXVgEgkOVHpOr6mpnZu"><div id="AccordionItem__46681" class="pxYchGNIM3U95N_8sY2T"><div class="BcPDQdbKyOolxjjq14w1"><div class="RichtextContent">It is recommended to have access to a computer with the capacity to handle the software that students use in their specialization.</div></div></div></div></div></li><li><div class="zsrYitxhmI4Rdxl8AcId te60PfIJAvlwZ2RBbGqe o80VkuFKdpLspcd2K6XW"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="AccordionItem__46682" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT GNG_gRf6Dl3NsaHoWAUO OyyOerhMVj5mV5WQNX5V xZxJs8W876NY1tCMuMwq UM1jfJqOS1COdaoBDFKC"><div class="YSRmfctHOQ5noBfQfMH5"><div class="DnD1xRazitrvmLCwsQvo"><h3 class="Y1lcLNcJwl0MgDDEuPIe">What can I study further?</h3></div><span class="SvgIcon MFUfNtxb_KMTBmiHESl8"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-plus"></use></svg></span></div></button><div style="will-change:height;overflow:hidden;visibility:hidden;height:0" class="ZgXVgEgkOVHpOr6mpnZu"><div id="AccordionItem__46682" class="pxYchGNIM3U95N_8sY2T"><div class="BcPDQdbKyOolxjjq14w1"><div class="RichtextContent">The program qualifies for admission to doctoral programs in artistic research.</div></div></div></div></div></li></ul></div></div></div></section><script>(window.__reactProps = window.__reactProps || {})['35c7a374-json'] = {"id":"frequently-asked-questions","heading":{"value":"Frequently asked questions</p>\n"},"accordionItems":[{"id":"95359","displayName":"What are the admission requirements?","introText":{"value":"A Master&rsquo;s degree in Design builds upon a bachelor&rsquo;s degree or other equivalent education amounting to 180 ECTS, with at least 80 ECTS relevant to the chosen specialization.</p>\n<p>For the specialization in Interior Architecture, a bachelor&rsquo;s degree in Interior Architecture is required.</p>\n<p>For the specialization in Visual Communication Design, applicants with a bachelor&rsquo;s degree in Graphic Design, Illustration, Art Direction, Interaction Design, Animation, or similar fields may apply.</p>\n<p>Kristiania may, in accordance with the<span>&nbsp;</span>Regulations on Requirements for Master&rsquo;s Degrees, approve other documented qualifications&mdash;such as relevant professional experience&mdash;that are wholly or partially equivalent to these requirements in special cases.<br /><br /><strong>Language requirements</strong><br />Applicants with education from outside the Nordic countries must document their proficiency in English, in terms of speaking and writing. You can meet the English language requirements by completing one of the following tests:&nbsp;</p>\n<ul class=\"Richtext__ul\">\n<li>English (140 hours) from Norwegian upper secondary school: written and oral exam.</li>\n<li>TOEFL with a minimum of 500 points from TOEFL PBT (paper-based test) or 60 points from TOEFL IBT (internet-based test).</li>\n<li>IELTS academic test with a minimum score of 5.0.</li>\n<li>PTE Academic, academic test with a minimum score of 51.</li>\n<li>Cambridge ESOL Examinations: First Certificate in English, Certificate in Advanced English, Certificate of Proficiency in English.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You can also meet the English requirements if you have completed one of the following:&nbsp;</p>\n<ul class=\"Richtext__ul\">\n<li>A university degree in English language and literature</li>\n<li>A minimum of one year of university studies taught in English in one of these countries: Australia, Canada, Ireland, New Zealand, Great Britain, or the USA.</li>\n<li>Completed a bachelor&rsquo;s degree where the language of instruction was English</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Separate admission requirements for the program &ndash; entrance exam</strong><br />The entrance exam is as follows:&nbsp;<br /><br /></p>\n<p>1. Application Letter that sets out the applicant's academic area of interest, goals,&nbsp;and motivation for applying to the program/specialization, as well as a&nbsp;preliminary description of the theme for the master's project. The heading must&nbsp;reflect the specialization the candidate is applying for. The application lettershould include:</p>\n<p>a. Motivation and goals for applying to the program.<br />b. Presentation of the desired theme for design exploration in the master's<br />project, including the background for your interest in the theme, the<br />theme's societal relevance, suggestions for a problem statement/research<br />questions that delimit the theme, methods/process frameworks, and<br />theory/knowledge base.</p>\n<p>The theme is not binding for the entire master's period but will guide the<br />assignment of your master's supervisor. The application letter should not exceed&nbsp;800 words.</p>\n<p>2. 3-6 Works Samples that demonstrate the applicant's artistic and academic level within the specialization they are applying for. Describe the themes and&nbsp;frameworks of the works/projects with a brief introduction. Explain the process&nbsp;and methods in at least one of the works. Work samples can be supplemented&nbsp;with attached files (e.g., video, audio, etc.) or a URL to a website where they are&nbsp;adequately presented.</p>\n<p>3. CV. The CV should detail education and work experience, independent<br />artistic/design activities, and other competencies/experience.</p>\n<p>4. Diplomas and/or Other Documentation of formal Competence in higher<br />education. This documentation must be submitted in two places, so the<br />admissions committee can assess the education as part of the admission<br />evaluation, and so the formal admission requirement is documented. These<br />documents must be stored separately in our systems.</p>\n<p>Applicants who qualify for the second admission round through the first round will be&nbsp;invited to a mandatory interview and/or additional admission test in the chosen&nbsp;specialization. Further information will accompany the invitation to the second&nbsp;admission round."},"callToAction":null,"linkAsButton":true},{"id":"95325","displayName":"What equipment will I need?","introText":{"value":"It is recommended to have access to a computer with the capacity to handle the software that students use in their specialization."},"callToAction":null,"linkAsButton":false},{"id":"95324","displayName":"What can I study further?","introText":{"value":"The program qualifies for admission to doctoral programs in artistic research."},"callToAction":null,"linkAsButton":false}]};</script></div>
</div></div>
    </div>
</article>

    </main>
</div>

